{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498107-mage-the-awakening-solo-play","id":1498107,"title":"Mage: the Awakening solo play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-26T19:42:33-08:00","id":1498107,"title":"Mage: the Awakening solo play","content":"Does anyone have any experience with running Mage the Awakening using the likes of an Ironsworn hack or the Mythic GM emulator? I play primarily in written form right now and a solo game to amuse myself when work is slow could prove very fun, but I'm worried that particular details like Surface/Deep Information might not fit very well into a &quot;yes/no&quot; question format.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T00:21:14-08:00","id":1498408,"title":"","content":"I have played Changeling the Lost 1e and 2e solo with the full rules while using Ironsworn Action/Theme, Location, Character tables, and the Progression Tracks. I do journaling a lot with it as well. I use only two moves called <i>Delve the Depths</i> in place of <i>Undertake a Journe</i>y and <i>Reveal a Danger</i>, from Ironsworn Delve book. I tweaked the <i>Delve the Depths</i> Moves with attribute+skills from CoD for traversing the outdoors and magical realms. Progression tracks are also great for traveling in the city as well. You can use Progression tracks just for about anything, like improving a relationship, seeing how long a weather is brewing, taking the time to do research, etc even with the CoD attribute+skills you roll with it. In the past I used all the Ironsworn Moves and they do work great as they help train you to narrate the story by yourself very well. After about a year and half, though, I was able to use just the tables and tracks. The Ironsworn Action/Theme table is the best to use as conversations/dialogues/rumors/telepathy with NPCs, events or to see what is happening in the area you are in, and many more. I usually like to roll the Action/Theme about 3 times to see what a NPC is saying, even though it might be a bit slow. It gives a lot of information with the first thing on your mind to interpret what they say. I also use tables from other RPGs to enrich it. The Yes/No question is still incredibly useful as well! I have no experience with Mythic GM Emulator, though. Mage the Awakening sounds like a fun game to solo! I might consider trying it someday. I hope this helps and best of luck to you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","user":"Omichli","date":". 11-30-2022, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T22:11:40-08:00","id":1499193,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the feedback, I'm also a big Ironsworn fan. I've been using MUNE and UNE for various RPG's since this post and have found them to be perfectly compatible.<br /> <br /> if people are curious, I can explain more about how it all works. I'm basically STing for myself in a play-by-post game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T22:17:32-08:00","id":1499194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498107-mage-the-awakening-solo-play?p=1499193#post1499193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the feedback, I'm also a big Ironsworn fan. I've been using MUNE and UNE for various RPG's since this post and have found them to be perfectly compatible.<br /> <br /> if people are curious, I can explain more about how it all works. I'm basically STing for myself in a play-by-post game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like an explanation, if you don't mind. I doubt I'm going to get my gaming group together for a while, so solo play might be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T22:39:11-08:00","id":1499195,"title":"","content":"MUNE is a free &quot;GM Emulator&quot; / &quot;Oracle&quot; system. It responds to Yes/No questions with &quot;Yes, No, Yes And, No And, Yes But&quot; or &quot;No But&quot; responses on a d6 roll. There's a few other tables to roll on, as well, based on the context of the circumstance I'm in -- but the gist of it is that you ask questions to get answers, and interpret the answers you get based on the context they're given in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mJbHcCNscMfs_NPnqMMz2Y8KiD8gWrkZ/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mJbHcCNscMfs_NPnqMMz2Y8KiD8gWrkZ/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mJbHcCNscMfs_NPnqMMz2Y8KiD8gWrkZ/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mJbHcCNscMfs_NPnqMMz2Y8KiD8gWrkZ/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This document explains how it works. I don't use a random word generator, instead using some 1d100 table for &quot;action&quot; and &quot;verb&quot; to create a two-word prompt.<br /> <br /> For instance, I might ask &quot;What does the Heirarch ask me to do?&quot; and get &quot;Murder Bureaucracy,&quot; and decide that he's asked me to duck under the red tape that's stopping him from doing something important and do it in his stead. Or maybe he needs me to take a sleeper politician out of the picture. Whichever jumps to mind first, I run with.<br /> <br /> I try to rely on the M:tA 2nd ed system whenever I can. For instance, I don't ask &quot;Do I lose my pursuers?&quot;in a chase scene, I roll Dex+Drive. I only use MUNE to emulate having a GM, helping to shape the plot and set the scene.<br /> <br /> UNE is the Universal NPC Emulator: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134163/UNE-The-Universal-NPC-Emulator-rev\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...C-Emulator-rev</a><br /> <br /> It helps generate details for NPCs using a series of d100 rolls, including power level relative to the PC, and what mood they're currently in. It works similarly to the two-word prompt system; creating prompts for my imagination. Whatever comes to mind first, I run with.<br /> <br /> Used appropriately, these two tools can fuel entire campaigns of fun. In particular, I'm very careful to only ask questions and use the emulators when my character would become aware of the information. I don't ask &quot;Did that tremere steal my sister's soul?&quot; I instead ask &quot;Does my Death sight reveal soulnessness in my sister?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T22:46:01-08:00","id":1499196,"title":"","content":"